# aqualog2nc: Convert data in Origin Pro-type OPJ files containing Horiba AquaLog EEM+Absorbance to NetCDF files.
-----------------------------

## STATUS
-----------------------------

A few things to know:
1. This project is entirely based on LLM-generated code (I don't know C++). But I do love open science, and this led me to want to "free" Aqualog data from the proprietary OPJ files to NetCDF.
2. The project is not finished and not properly documented (as of August 2026). 
3. The format of the NetCDF file might change slowly over time until v1.0 is released.
4. Use at your own risk. Get involved to speed things up! (see to do).
5. Only unprocessed data is grabed and exported. You'll need to replicate the processing yourself (it's a feature, not a bug).

Working:
1. The tool converts EEM 3D + Absorbance sheets to NetCDF Attributes and Variables
2. The folder is scanned for OPJ and OGW files automatically and any samples are aggregated into one NetCDF file
3. Settings mismatches are handled automatically: If settings are equal, the file stores in the root of the NetCDF, otherwise samples are grouped into batches.
4. Blanks are detected and discarded (if left in OPJ as seperate samples)
5. Incomplete (i.e. aborted) samples will be tossed, the routine checks dimenions and completeness.
6. Based on a sampling campaign consisting of ~200 samples, the fully processed EEMs and absorbance spectra (processed from NetCDF files using the drEEM toolbox) are within machine precision of the "HJY Export" reference.


## USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:
-----------------------------

1. macOS (Apple Silicon only):
	- Download aqualog2nc-macos-arm64
	- Double click on aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 (do not move to trash when promted)
	- Go to Settings -> Security & Privacy -> scroll down -> approve the application
	- Open terminal -> change to directory containing aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 -> run "chmod +x aqualog2nc-macos-arm64"  (making the software exectutable)
	- Usage: ./aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 <input.opj | input_folder> output.nc (e.g. ./aqualog2nc-macos-arm64 /Users/wuensch/test.opj test.nc)
	- NetCDF file will appear in the current directory of the terminal (not the directory with the OPJ files)

2. Windows
	- Download aqualog2nc-windows-x64.exe
	- Open the executable -> On the blue pop-up, click "more info" -> Run anyway
	- Open Terminal -> change to directory containing aqualog2nc-windows-x64.exe
	- Usage: ./aqualog2nc-windows-x64 <input.opj | input_folder> output.nc (e.g. ./aqualog2nc-windows-x64 "C:\Users\Public\Documents\Jobin Yvon\" test.nc)
	- NetCDF file will appear in the current directory of the terminal (not the directory with the OPJ files)

3. Linux
	I don't have a machine running Linux, so I could not produce a walk-through. Expect it to be similar to macOS.

## GETTING INVOLVED
-----------------------------

Contributions, bug reports, and feature requests are welcome.

If you encounter a problem, please open a GitHub issue and include:

- Your operating system and version
- The aqualog2nc release version
- A description of the problem
- Any error messages produced by the program
- A sample OPJ file, if you want me to fix the issue quickly


## ATTRIBUTION
-----------------------------

aqualog2nc is derived from the liborigin project:

https://github.com/gerlachs/liborigin

liborigin is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3 (GPL-3.0).

aqualog2nc extends liborigin with support for extracting Horiba AquaLog
EEM and absorbance data and exporting the results to NetCDF.

Original liborigin authors include Stefan Gerlach and contributors.
